<title>UK: Lower prices fail to attract UK meals buyers.</title>
<headline>Lower prices fail to attract UK meals buyers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lower asking prices failed to attract buyers on the UK meals and feeds market on Friday.</p>
<p>Brokers said most players were awaiting the USDA crop report, but this contained no surprises.</p>
<p>Lower Chicago futures on near ideal growing conditions added to the lack of interest.</p>
<p>High protein soymeal offers were around three to four stg lower while most other sectors of the market were unchanged.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
